-- Tauren 4 metres tall (VoldemarGreed "bugs 6", 2026-11-17: the purple-robed Twilight tauren in Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight
-- Elementalist 4814 and friends). The old data (TDB and the VMaNGOS import) gives tauren creatures DisplayScale 1.35 (male) or 1.25
-- (female). That was the tauren race size: the old server also made tauren PLAYERS 1.35 / 1.25 tall, so creature and player matched.
-- Our client draws tauren at full size by itself (players get scale 1, the tauren models have CreatureModelScale 1 and ModelScale 1),
-- so these creatures came out 35% bigger than a tauren player. Live sniffs agree: all 570 sniffed rows on tauren displays have
-- DisplayScale 1 (e.g. Boarton Shadetotem 205729, Earthen Ring Shaman 257862).
-- Fix: DisplayScale = old value / race size (1.35 male model, 1.25 female model), for every unsniffed row (VerifiedBuild < 50000) on
-- a tauren display (CreatureDisplayInfoExtra DisplayRaceID 6) that is not 1. Creatures meant to be bigger or smaller keep that:
-- Huum Wildmane 1.5 -> 1.11, Twilight Loreseeker 1.15 -> 0.85. Rows sniffed on live are not touched.
-- Each row only changes while it still holds the old value, so it is safe to run again.
UPDATE `creature_template_model` SET `DisplayScale` = 1 WHERE `CreatureID` = 646 AND `Idx` = 0 AND `CreatureDisplayID` = 2026 AND ABS(`DisplayScale` - 1.35) < 0.001; -- 1.35 / 1.35 male, Mr. Smite
UPDATE `creature_template_model` SET `DisplayScale` = 1 WHERE `CreatureID` = 2478 AND `Idx` = 0 AND `CreatureDisplayID` = 3442 AND ABS(`DisplayScale` - 1.35) < 0.001; -- 1.35 / 1.35 male, Haren Swifthoof
